IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`

-- Old Age Security Act, section 2 (Interpretation): the defined terms that name a person, a payment or an
-- event: applicant, beneficiary, pensioner, survivor, common-law partner, cheque, release, and the Part under
-- which each benefit is authorized. Each rule works the term out from facts the person can state; nothing in
-- it asks the caller to decide what the term means.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- "applicant means a person who has applied, or is deemed to have applied, for a benefit, or with respect to
-- whom an application for a benefit has been waived"
-- ("application means an application for a benefit": the word is carried by the first input below.)
-- src:17 | applicant means a person who has applied, or is deemed to have applied, for a benefit, or with respect to whom an application for a benefit has been waived; (demandeur)
-- src:18 | application means an application for a benefit; (Version anglaise seulement)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 2 "applicant", "application" (src:17-18)
GIVEN `the person has applied for a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is deemed to have applied for a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement for an application for a benefit has been waived in respect of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is an applicant` `the person has applied for a benefit` `the person is deemed to have applied for a benefit` `the requirement for an application for a benefit has been waived in respect of the person` MEANS
        `the person has applied for a benefit`
    OR  `the person is deemed to have applied for a benefit`
    OR  `the requirement for an application for a benefit has been waived in respect of the person`

-- "beneficiary means a person to whom payment of a benefit has been approved"
-- src:19 | beneficiary means a person to whom payment of a benefit has been approved; (prestataire)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 2 "beneficiary" (src:19)
GIVEN `payment of a benefit has been approved for the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is a beneficiary` `payment of a benefit has been approved for the person` MEANS
    `payment of a benefit has been approved for the person`

-- "pensioner means a person whose application for a pension has been approved"
-- src:64 | pensioner means a person whose application for a pension has been approved; (pensionné)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 2 "pensioner" (src:64)
GIVEN `the person's application for a pension has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is a pensioner` `the person's application for a pension has been approved` MEANS
    `the person's application for a pension has been approved`

-- "survivor means a person whose spouse or common-law partner has died and who has not thereafter become
-- the spouse or common-law partner of another person". "Spouse" is no longer defined in the Act (the
-- definition was repealed in 2000), so the spouse is a fact the person states.
-- src:84 | survivor means a person whose spouse or common-law partner has died and who has not thereafter become the spouse or common-law partner of another person. (survivant)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 2 "survivor" (src:84)
GIVEN `the person's spouse or common-law partner has died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has since become the spouse or common-law partner of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is a survivor` `the person's spouse or common-law partner has died` `the person has since become the spouse or common-law partner of another person` MEANS
        `the person's spouse or common-law partner has died`
    AND (NOT `the person has since become the spouse or common-law partner of another person`)

-- "common-law partner, in relation to an individual, means a person who is cohabiting with the individual in a
-- conjugal relationship at the relevant time, having so cohabited with the individual for a continuous period
-- of at least one year. For greater certainty, in the case of an individual's death, the "relevant time"
-- means the time of the individual's death"
--
-- The relevant time is the day the individual died if they have died, and otherwise the day as at which the
-- question is asked (the day of an application, the first day of a month, and so on). A continuous period of
-- cohabitation of at least one year is one that began on or before the day one year before the relevant time:
-- the anniversary day counts (fork F6 in NOTES.md).
-- src:22 | common-law partner, in relation to an individual, means a person who is cohabiting with the individual in a conjugal relationship at the relevant time, having so cohabited with the individual for a continuous period of at least one year. For greater certainty, in the case of an individual’s death, the “relevant time” means the time of the individual’s death; (conjoint de fait)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 2 "common-law partner" (src:22)
GIVEN `the person is cohabiting with the individual in a conjugal relationship at the relevant time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the continuous period of cohabitation began` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the individual died` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is a common-law partner of the individual` `the person is cohabiting with the individual in a conjugal relationship at the relevant time` `the day on which the continuous period of cohabitation began` `the day on which the individual died` `the day as at which the question is asked` MEANS
        `the person is cohabiting with the individual in a conjugal relationship at the relevant time`
    AND `add years` `the day on which the continuous period of cohabitation began` 1 AT MOST `the relevant time`
    WHERE
        `the relevant time` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which the individual died`
            WHEN JUST day THEN day
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day as at which the question is asked`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- "cheque means any instrument issued in payment of a benefit"
-- src:21 | cheque means any instrument issued in payment of a benefit; (chèque)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 2 "cheque" (src:21)
GIVEN `the instrument was issued in payment of a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the instrument is a cheque` `the instrument was issued in payment of a benefit` MEANS
    `the instrument was issued in payment of a benefit`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- "release, in relation to a person who has been incarcerated, means release from custody on earned
-- remission, at the expiry of a sentence, or on parole or statutory release that has not been terminated or
-- revoked"
--
-- The words "that has not been terminated or revoked" are read as qualifying both "parole" and "statutory
-- release" (fork F7 in NOTES.md).
DECLARE `Manner of release` IS ONE OF
    `Release on earned remission`
    `Release at the expiry of a sentence`
    `Release on parole`
    `Release on statutory release`
    `Any other release from custody`

-- src:66 | release, in relation to a person who has been incarcerated, means release from custody on earned remission, at the expiry of a sentence, or on parole or statutory release that has not been terminated or revoked. (libération)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 2 "release" (src:66)
GIVEN `the way the person left custody` IS A `Manner of release`
      `the parole or statutory release has been terminated or revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`leaving custody in this way is a release` `the way the person left custody` `the parole or statutory release has been terminated or revoked` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the way the person left custody`
    WHEN `Release on earned remission`           THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Release at the expiry of a sentence`   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Release on parole`                     THEN NOT `the parole or statutory release has been terminated or revoked`
    WHEN `Release on statutory release`          THEN NOT `the parole or statutory release has been terminated or revoked`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- "allowance means the allowance authorized to be paid under Part III", "pension means a monthly pension
-- authorized to be paid under Part I", "supplement means a monthly guaranteed income supplement authorized to
-- be paid under Part II": the Part that authorizes each benefit. The conditions are in the Parts themselves,
-- which pieces oa1 (Part I) and oa2 (Parts II and III) encode.
-- src:16 | allowance means the allowance authorized to be paid under Part III; (allocation)
-- src:63 | pension means a monthly pension authorized to be paid under Part I; (pension)
-- src:83 | supplement means a monthly guaranteed income supplement authorized to be paid under Part II; (supplément)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 2 "allowance", "pension", "supplement" (src:16) (src:63) (src:83)
GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Part of the Act under which the benefit is authorized` benefit MEANS
    CONSIDER benefit
    WHEN Pension    THEN 1
    WHEN Supplement THEN 2
    WHEN Allowance  THEN 3
